  "solution": {
    "text": "Let $S=\\{1,2,3\\} \\Rightarrow n(S)=3$\nNow, $P(S)=$ set of all subsets of $S$ total no. of subsets $=2^3=8$\n$$\n\\therefore n[P(S)]=8\n$$\nNow, number of one-to-one functions from\n$$\nS \\rightarrow P(S) \\text { is }{ }^8 P_3=\\frac{8 !}{5 !}=8 \\times 7 \\times 6=336 .\n$$",
